{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "New Interests and Aspirations"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Registering for the Course"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe  necessity, duty, advice, or strong dissaproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le04ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Expressing Necessity in the Present and in the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modals must and have (got) to to express necessity in in the present and in the past. <br/> You use the negative forms of the modals <span class=\"italic\">need </span>to and <span class=\"italic\">have to </span>to express absence of necessity in the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Must</span> refers to a necessary condition that comes from the subject and may be directed at the subject or the person the subject is talking to or about. It is used to express a strong necessity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br><ul><span class=\"italic\">First, you must present three pieces of ID.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have (got)  to</span> expresses external obligations, which come from outside of the subject. These may be rules and regulations over which the subject has no control. It is used to express necessity in a lower degree than with <span class=\"italic\">must</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br><ul><span class=\"italic\">If you want to pass this course, you have to keep on top of your assignments.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of necessity is expressed with the <span class=\"strong\">negative form of have to</span>, not with <span class=\"italic\">mustn't</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><ul><span class=\"italic\">You don't have to select all your core subjects this semester.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can only express necessity in the past with the modal have to. <br/> Structure: <br/> <ul>subject + had to + infinitive"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/> <ul><span class=\"italic\">I had to drop out of one of my classes last semester.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of necessity is expressed with the<span class=\"strong\"> negative form of have to </span>in the past. <br/> To express absence of necessity in the past, you use the structure: <br/><ul> subject+didn't + have/need + infinitive."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><ul><span class=\"italic\">Food and Beverage Management was an easy course. I didn't have to work too hard on that subject.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of necessity can also be expressed by negative form of <span class=\"italic\">need</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "First you must present three pieces of ID and a document from your last school, as well as your student number."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do I have to have proof of address?"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I have selected the three core courses that I have to take."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I must inform you that, as of today, if you drop or withdraw from that course in particular."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Clarifying your opinion "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use linking expressions to express your position and to show how ideas are connected. You use linking expressions to clarify your opinion."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discourse markers can show a <span class=\"strong\">connection </span>to what you want to say and what was said before. They can also show your position and opinion on a particular situation. <br/> Linking expressions are used to further explain and clarify your opinion or position on a subject. They follow a previous statement or sentence and build on that idea."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/> <ul><span class=\"italic\">By this I mean ... </span> <br/><span class=\"italic\"> I'm referring to ...</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">To be honest ...</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">That is to say ...</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm referring to the transcript from your last school."}, {"type": "example", "content": "By that I mean that there are numerous reports, essays and seminars."}, {"type": "example", "content": "To be honest I'm not sure if I should choose Food and Beverage Management because I took something similar at Culinary school ."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "transcript"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an \u200bexact written \u200bcopy of something, as in grades from University, college or high school"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must present three pieces of ID and a transcript from your last school."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about college and university."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "budgeting"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bprocess of \u200bcalculating how much \u200bmoney you must \u200bearn or \u200bsave during a particular \u200bperiod of \u200btime, and of \u200bplanning how you will \u200bspend it: "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you take Food and Beverage you'll learn a lot about budgeting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proof of address"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a document in which your name and address are indicated clearly to prove you do live there"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do I have to have proof of address?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to drop a course"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dropping a class during the refund/schedule adjustment period means the student no longer wishes to attend the class and wishes to receive a refund"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I must inform you that, as of today, if you drop that course in particular, you won't receive a refund."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "full course load"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "generally, a full load in most semester-based classes at the undergraduate level is four to five classes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many students have found it difficult to take a full course load when that course is part of it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "workload"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bamount of \u200bwork to be done, \u200bespecially by a \u200bparticular \u200bperson or \u200bmachine in a \u200bperiod of \u200btime"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Will you tell me which courses have the biggest work load?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "essay"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200bshort \u200bpiece of writing on a \u200bparticular \u200bsubject, \u200bespecially one done by \u200bstudents as \u200bpart of the \u200bwork for a \u200bcourse "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That course has numerous reports, essays and seminars."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to keep on top of"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stay well-informed about the status of someone or something. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to keep on top of your assignments and you must not get behind."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be all set"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be prepared, ready, or primed to begin or complete a task at hand"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, you're all set!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud10"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to withdraw from a course"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "withdrawing from a class means the student no longer wishes to attend the class but will not receive a refund because the refund/schedule adjustment period has ended"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I must inform you that, as of today, if you withdraw from that course in particular, you won't receive a refund."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reread the dialogue paying attention to the vocabulary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell someone what you need to present or show them in order to express what's necessary in registering for your school, college, etc. (use must, have to mustn't)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to step by step registration instructions online."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about education registration"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express what's necessary in registering for a school, college, etc."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen to a step by step registration process in English."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le04ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le04ob07re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le04ob07re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Hi. I'm here to register for my classes.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: First you must present three pieces of ID and a document from your last school, as well as your student number.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le04ob07re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Which document?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: I'm referring to the transcript from your last school.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Okay. Do I have to have proof of address?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: No. These are fine. Okay, so which courses have you selected in your program?", "id": 2, "time": "10500", "image": "engenn10le04ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I have selected the three core courses that I have to take, but not the electives. To be honest I'm not sure if I should choose Food and Beverage Management because I took something similar at Culinary school .<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: If you take Food and Beverage you'll learn a lot about budgeting, specifically for smaller restaurants.", "id": 3, "time": "25000", "image": "engenn10le04ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: It seems to me that would be beneficial. I'll sign up for that elective and the one called Advanced Wine Studies and Management before they are full.", "id": 4, "time": "45000", "image": "engenn10le04ob07re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: Okay,  I must inform you that, as of today, if you drop or withdraw from that course in particular, you won't receive a refund. When you commit to that course, it's permanent, because it is so popular and limited to a small number of students. As soon as you are enrolled in all five courses, you will receive confirmation via email.", "id": 5, "time": "55000", "image": "engenn10le04ob07re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: In case I forget, will you tell me which courses have the biggest work load?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Registrar</span>: Yes. If you ask me, Management and Food operations seems the heaviest. By that I mean that there are numerous reports, essays and seminars. Many students have found it difficult to take a full course load when that course is part of it. You have to keep on top of your assignments and you must not get behind. Well, you're all set! Before you leave please use the computer in the foyer and enter your student number to activate enrollment.", "id": 6, "time": "74000", "image": "engenn10le04ob07re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about education and character traits."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express what is and isn't necessary in the present and in the past."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can clarify my opinion. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do you know about the practice of meditation? Would you try it or recommend it?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What other things can you do to feel more relaxed?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback